I replaced the linear scan with a one-time-built 65536-entry pointer lookup table, so each call becomes a single indexed load. The table preserves first-match semantics and returns `NULL` for unknown message numbers.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* table[65536];
    static bool init = false;

    if (!init)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
        {
            if (table[mesgs[i].num] == NULL)
                table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        init = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```